DELIVERY: OPT-11 implementation architecture/algorithm contract completed (documentation only; OPT-11 still not released).

Commit: ed15787 (docs: add OPT-11 architecture and algorithms contract)

Artifact: docs/design/OPT_11_ARCHITECTURE_AND_ALGORITHMS.md

It gives Gemini concrete implementation guidance for:
- non-negotiable ownership/lifetime/completion invariants;
- producer/bridge/worker/job/plugin roles and owner-thread guard;
- RenderWorker state machine and typed commands/acks;
- bounded SPSC snapshot queue with protected-frame policy and memory ordering;
- render-worker loop, transactional resize, device-loss and shutdown algorithms;
- RenderGraph DAG construction, deterministic topological sort, lifetime intervals, first-fit interval coloring, alias events and publish-after-submit commit;
- NRI parallel-recording capability probe, DAG-level partitioning, allocator isolation, deterministic merge and serial/CPU-preparation fallback;
- plugin unload boundary, failure matrix, implementation order, forbidden shortcuts and completion checklist.

Validation: git diff --check (exit 0); python -m json.tool docs/agents/CODEX_GEMINI_EXCHANGE.json (exit 0); referenced design files exist. No build/test run because this commit is documentation-only.

HANDOFF: User has now released OPT-11 package C11-01 only, with an explicit one-package/one-commit rule.

Package: C11-01 / 11.1 Ownership design and capability probes
Base commit: 73a8971
Implementer: Gemini
Reviewer: Codex consolidated final review

Required scope:
- bind RenderService/RHIDevice/resource/presentation ownership to one declared render owner;
- add worker state/capability reporting and wrong-owner-thread guards;
- define startup/surface/device-loss/shutdown transitions and preserve synchronous fallback;
- audit callers of CanSubmit/resource creation/WaitIdle/resize/present so producer paths do not issue native calls;
- add focused CPU/fault-injection tests and package documentation/evidence.

Stop boundary: do not implement C11-02 snapshot queue, C11-03 worker presentation, C11-04 parallel recording, C11-05 aliasing, C11-06 stress or C11-07 acceptance in this handoff. Use the architecture contract in docs/design/OPT_11_ARCHITECTURE_AND_ALGORITHMS.md and the execution plan in docs/design/OPT_11_EXECUTION_PLAN.md. Report exact files, base/head commits, commands, exit codes and unavailable native gates; label the result implemented/self-verified pending Codex review.
